sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant U as User
  participant M as Native App
  participant B as System Browser
  participant A as ReadyPackets Authorization Server
  participant I as Entra ID (optional)
  participant API as ReadyPackets Mobile API
  participant D as Session & Device Store

  U->>M: Select Sign in
  M->>M: Generate PKCE verifier, challenge, state, nonce
  M->>B: Start authorization request
  B->>A: GET /authorize (PKCE challenge, redirect URI)
  alt Local ReadyPackets account
    A->>U: Present hosted sign-in and MFA
  else Entra SAML account
    A->>I: Redirect to enterprise SSO
    I->>A: Validated SAML assertion
    A->>U: Apply ReadyPackets MFA policy where required
  end
  A->>B: Redirect to claimed app link with authorization code and state
  B->>M: Return to verified universal/app link
  M->>A: POST /token (code + PKCE verifier)
  A->>D: Create device-bound refresh-token family and session record
  A-->>M: Short-lived access token + rotated refresh token
  M->>M: Store refresh token in Keychain or Keystore and keep access token in memory
  M->>API: HTTPS request + Bearer access token + idempotency key where required
  API->>D: Validate token, device, MFA state, role, and revocation status
  API-->>M: Authorized, versioned response DTO
  Note over M,API: Refresh rotation detects reuse and revokes the token family
